# Honesty + security copy

## Do

- Match UI status to real artifacts (registry tx, x402 receipt, labeled set path, WASM binary).
- Use “resistance to gaming” with linked adversarial tests.
- Prefer “calibrated / proper scoring / Brier” with methodology over absolute claims.
- Keep marketing and app console separate in tone: product truth over theater.

## Don’t

- Invent labeled-set sizes, agreement scores, request counts, or checksums.
- Mark roadmap items done without on-chain/API evidence.
- Use invented YAML fields (`vertical.verify`) — only GitBook canonical schema.
- Claim “unhackable,” “cannot be gamed,” or “even nation-state attackers can’t.”
- Ship Cosplay dashboards to Discord/judges as if live.

## Example

```tsx
// ❌ BAD
<meta>4,128 labeled rows</meta> // when no dataset exists

// ✅ GOOD
<meta>Labeled holdout: pending lock — see memory/VERTICAL_CANDIDATES.md</meta>
```
